    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full `mvn test` run is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` feature for `POST /api/owners`: when a request includes `birthDate` (ISO), the owner's `ageBand` (`MINOR` <18, `ADULT` 18\u201364, `SENIOR` 65+) is derived against the `registrationDate`.\n\nBecause the acceptance test creates the owner and reads `ageBand` back via a separate `GET`, `birthDate` had to be persisted and the band computed at response time \u2014 matching how the existing derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `locality`, `checkDigit`, \u2026) already work.\n\nChanges, each in its natural place:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` to `OwnerFields` (input + persisted/returned) and a read-only `ageBand` to `Owner`. DTOs regenerate from this.\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 new `birthDate` column with getter/setter, alongside `registrationDate`.\n3. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility helper `AgeBand.on(birthDate, registrationDate)` holding the sole band definition, mirroring the existing `CheckDigit`/`CustomerCode` helpers. Returns `null` when either date is absent.\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 a one-line `ageBand(owner)` mapping delegating to `AgeBand`, consistent with the other derived-field expressions. `birthDate` maps by name automatically through `toOwner`/`toOwnerDto`, so it flows request \u2192 entity \u2192 response with no extra wiring.\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema).\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function step was needed: `BuildOwner` already maps the request DTO to the entity, and `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate`/`ApplyOwnerRegistrationDate` already establish the `registrationDate` the band is measured against.",
